Functions of the Secretary. The Secretary shall have the following functions:
(a) Establish the internal organization of the departments, its bureau and office to achieve its functions and
objectives;
(b) Advise the President in the promulgation of executive orders, regulations, and decrees relative to matters
falling under the jurisdiction of the department;
(c) Establish the policies and standards for the operation of the department pursuant to the President's

programs of government;
(d) Promulgate rules and regulations necessary to carry out the department objectives, policies and functions;
(e) Exercise supervision and control over all bureaus and offices under the department;
(f) Delegate authority for the performance of any functions to officers and employees under his direction; and
(g) Perform such other functions as may be provided by law.
